WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.911
Week 28: Subjunctive: Doubt, Purpose, and Contingency. qualify certainty state purpose and conditions plan for contingencies

2
00:00:08.911 --> 00:00:28.497
Read for the situation. Es posible que el informe contenga errores. Antes de que el consejo vote, los analistas revisarán las fuentes para que todos comprendan los riesgos. The report may contain errors. Before the council votes, the analysts will review the sources so that everyone understands the risks.

3
00:00:28.497 --> 00:00:37.067
Read again for evidence. Identify who acts, what changes, when it happens, and which words establish the relationship between events.

4
00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:42.928
Reading activities. Reading activity 67; Reading activity 68

5
00:00:42.928 --> 00:00:50.709
Retell. Without looking back, give the main idea, three supporting details, and one reasonable inference in Spanish.

6
00:00:50.709 --> 00:01:18.097
Model language. Dudo que la cifra sea correcta. — I doubt that the figure is correct. Es probable que llueva esta noche. — It will probably rain tonight. Salimos temprano para que haya tiempo suficiente. — We are leaving early so that there is enough time. No firmaremos a menos que cambien la cláusula. — We will not sign unless they change the clause. Llámame en cuanto llegues. — Call me as soon as you arrive.

7
00:01:18.097 --> 00:01:27.846
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
